---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FlooringCostCalculator from '../../components/FlooringCostCalculator.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Flooring Cost Calculator: Vinyl Plank and Peel-and-Stick"
  description="Free flooring cost calculator: enter room size and floor type to see square feet to buy, materials cost and a rough pro labor range. No sign-up."
>
  <h1>Flooring cost calculator</h1>
  <p>
    Enter your room size, choose peel-and-stick tile or click-lock vinyl plank, and see how many square
    feet to buy plus a materials range and a rough professional labor range. Every price is editable, so
    you can plug in a real quote or a store listing. No sign-up, and nothing you type leaves your browser.
  </p>

  <FlooringCostCalculator length={12} width={10} />

  <h2>What the numbers include</h2>
  <p>
    The tool adds a waste allowance to your floor area (10% by default; sources we read range from 5% for a
    simple rectangle to 10-15% for diagonal layouts) and multiplies by the low and high price per square
    foot. Labor is a separate range, and the sources disagree a lot on it, which is why the plank range is
    wide. Removing an old floor, trim, transitions, leveling and subfloor repair are extras: the removal
    checkbox uses one guide's figure, and the rest are not included.
  </p>
  <p>
    A flat, clean, dry subfloor matters more than the product for how a floor lasts. Check the
    manufacturer's instructions, and if you rent, get written permission before installing anything.
  </p>

